WEBVTT

00:00:05.301 --> 00:00:10.098
DIVINE MAGIC
BY LIMA CARNEIRO

00:00:11.182 --> 00:00:12.308
(BARKING)

00:00:12.975 --> 00:00:14.811
-(TIRES SCREECH)
-(HORN BLARING)

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:20.316
MAN 1: Hey, you all right there?

00:00:21.818 --> 00:00:23.986
-(HORSE WHINNYING)
-MAN 2: Whoa!

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.202
(HISSING)

00:00:37.792 --> 00:00:38.793
(CREATURE SCREECHING)

00:00:41.129 --> 00:00:42.588
(PHONES RINGING)

00:00:42.839 --> 00:00:43.840
(ELEVATOR BELL DINGS)

00:00:45.925 --> 00:00:48.302
And so this is the newsroom.

00:00:48.469 --> 00:00:49.554
Let's go.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:51.848
Hey, how are you?

00:00:52.932 --> 00:00:54.684
Make way for the Barebones.

00:00:56.352 --> 00:00:58.521
Now, they're just
putting the papers to bed,

00:00:58.688 --> 00:01:00.231
as they say.

00:01:00.857 --> 00:01:01.858
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:01:04.569 --> 00:01:07.113
Mr. Shaw. Sir. He's with the Senator.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:09.699
Never mind that, Barker.
I wanna see my father.

00:01:12.451 --> 00:01:14.245
I'm so sorry, Mr. Shaw,
but your son insisted.

00:01:14.412 --> 00:01:15.621
Father, you're gonna wanna hear this.

00:01:18.541 --> 00:01:21.377
(LAUGHS) I've got something huge.

00:01:21.669 --> 00:01:23.713
SHAW SENIOR: Your brother and I
are busy here, Langdon.

00:01:23.921 --> 00:01:25.214
Working on his election campaign.

00:01:25.381 --> 00:01:26.966
We don't have time for this.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:30.970
LANGDON: This is Mary Lou Barebone
from the New Salem Preservation Society.

00:01:31.387 --> 00:01:32.889
And she's got a big story for you.

00:01:34.432 --> 00:01:35.892
Oh, she has, has she?

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.561
LANGDON: There's strange things
going on all over the city.

00:01:38.728 --> 00:01:41.355
The people behind this,
they are not like you and me.

00:01:41.522 --> 00:01:43.482
This is witchcraft. Don't you see?

00:01:43.649 --> 00:01:45.651
-SHAW SENIOR: Langdon.
-She doesn't want any money.

00:01:46.652 --> 00:01:49.572
Then either her story is worthless,
or she's lying about the cost.

00:01:49.739 --> 00:01:51.824
Nobody gives away anything
valuable for free, Langdon.

00:01:51.991 --> 00:01:53.242
MARY LOU: You're right, Mr. Shaw.

00:01:53.659 --> 00:01:56.704
What we desire is infinitely
more valuable than money.

00:01:57.413 --> 00:01:58.414
It's your influence.

00:01:58.915 --> 00:02:01.167
Millions of people read your newspapers,

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:03.336
and they need to be made aware
about this danger.

00:02:03.753 --> 00:02:06.255
The crazy disturbances in the subway.

00:02:06.881 --> 00:02:07.924
Just look at the pictures.

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:09.926
SHAW SENIOR: I'd like
you and your friends to leave.

00:02:10.718 --> 00:02:13.179
No. Look, you're missing a trick here.
Just look at the evidence!

00:02:13.596 --> 00:02:14.597
SHAW SENIOR: Really?

00:02:14.764 --> 00:02:17.099
SENATOR SHAW: Langdon.
Listen to Father and just go.

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:18.851
And...

00:02:20.436 --> 00:02:21.479
Take the freaks with you.

00:02:21.646 --> 00:02:23.439
LANGDON: This is Father's office,
not yours.

00:02:23.606 --> 00:02:24.815
And I'm sick of this.
Every time I walk in here--

00:02:24.982 --> 00:02:26.192
SHAW SENIOR: Okay. That's it!

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.694
Thank you.

00:02:31.989 --> 00:02:34.116
We hope you'll reconsider, Mr. Shaw.

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:37.411
We're not difficult to find.

00:02:38.246 --> 00:02:39.997
Until then,

00:02:40.164 --> 00:02:41.791
we thank you for your time.

00:02:53.678 --> 00:02:54.887
Hey, boy!

00:02:56.847 --> 00:02:58.307
You dropped something.

00:03:02.019 --> 00:03:03.896
-(PAPER CRUMPLING)
-Here you go, freak.

00:03:04.063 --> 00:03:06.649
Why don't you put that in the trash
where you all belong?

00:03:16.784 --> 00:03:18.160
Take a right here.

00:03:21.414 --> 00:03:23.666
(JACOB GROANING)

00:03:27.962 --> 00:03:29.088
Okay.

00:03:29.422 --> 00:03:30.423
Before we go in...

00:03:30.589 --> 00:03:32.883
I'm not supposed to have men
on the premises.

00:03:33.301 --> 00:03:35.636
In that case, Mr. Kowalski and I
can easily seek other accommodations.

00:03:35.803 --> 00:03:37.013
-No, you don't.
-(JACOB GRUNTS)

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:39.056
-Watch your step.
-(GROANS)

00:03:45.229 --> 00:03:46.814
MRS. ESPOSITO: That you, Tina?

00:03:46.981 --> 00:03:47.982
Shh.

00:03:48.858 --> 00:03:50.568
Yes, Mrs. Esposito.

00:03:50.735 --> 00:03:51.861
MRS. ESPOSITO: Are you alone?

00:03:52.653 --> 00:03:54.822
I'm always alone, Mrs. Esposito.

00:03:57.575 --> 00:03:58.993
(1920s MUSIC PLAYING ON RADIO)

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:00.161
Oh...

00:04:01.704 --> 00:04:02.705
(DOOR CLOSES)

00:04:05.416 --> 00:04:06.417
(CHUCKLES)

00:04:08.502 --> 00:04:09.628
QUEENIE: Teenie,

00:04:09.879 --> 00:04:11.422
you brought men home.

00:04:13.549 --> 00:04:15.801
Gentlemen, this is my sister.

00:04:18.637 --> 00:04:20.056
Wanna put something on, Queenie?

00:04:20.389 --> 00:04:21.724
Oh, sure.

00:04:37.448 --> 00:04:40.242
So, who are they?

00:04:40.409 --> 00:04:41.619
That's Mr. Scamander.

00:04:41.786 --> 00:04:45.122
He's committed a serious infraction
of the National Statute of Secrecy.

00:04:45.873 --> 00:04:47.500
-He's a criminal?
-Uh-huh.

00:04:47.666 --> 00:04:49.585
And that's Mr. Kowalski. He's a No-Maj.

00:04:50.419 --> 00:04:51.587
QUEENIE: A No-Maj?

00:04:52.254 --> 00:04:53.923
Teen, what are you up to?

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.467
He's sick. It's a long story.

00:04:57.593 --> 00:05:01.263
Mr. Scamander has lost something
I'm going to help him find.

00:05:01.555 --> 00:05:02.556
Oh...

00:05:02.807 --> 00:05:03.974
You need to sit down, honey.

00:05:04.141 --> 00:05:06.018
He hasn't eaten anything all day.

00:05:06.268 --> 00:05:07.269
And--

00:05:07.812 --> 00:05:09.021
Oh, that's rough.

00:05:09.772 --> 00:05:11.690
He didn't get the money
he wanted for his bakery.

00:05:11.857 --> 00:05:12.942
You bake, honey?

00:05:13.776 --> 00:05:14.777
Uh...

00:05:15.027 --> 00:05:16.612
I love to cook.

00:05:16.779 --> 00:05:18.489
-You're a Legilimens?
-QUEENIE: Mmm. Yeah.

00:05:18.781 --> 00:05:21.492
But I always have trouble
with your kind. Brits.

00:05:21.951 --> 00:05:23.202
It's the accent.

00:05:24.161 --> 00:05:25.871
You know how to read minds?

00:05:26.288 --> 00:05:27.790
Oh, don't worry, honey.

00:05:27.957 --> 00:05:30.960
Most guys think what you was thinking
first time they see me.

00:05:33.087 --> 00:05:35.798
Now, you need food.

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:39.093
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

00:05:39.468 --> 00:05:41.470
(BUZZING)

00:05:44.807 --> 00:05:46.517
(CHITTERING)

00:05:48.978 --> 00:05:51.397
QUEENIE: Hot dog? Again?
TINA: Don't read my mind.

00:05:51.564 --> 00:05:52.940
QUEENIE: Not a very wholesome lunch.

00:05:56.318 --> 00:05:57.778
(MUSIC CONTINUES, INDISTINCT)

00:06:06.412 --> 00:06:07.413
Hey, Mr. Scamander.

00:06:11.876 --> 00:06:13.586
You prefer pie or strudel?

00:06:16.672 --> 00:06:18.674
I really don't have a preference.

00:06:24.013 --> 00:06:25.473
You prefer strudel, huh, honey?

00:06:26.682 --> 00:06:27.725
(CHUCKLES)

00:06:27.933 --> 00:06:29.101
Strudel it is.

00:06:45.743 --> 00:06:47.703
(INHALES DEEPLY)

00:06:48.871 --> 00:06:50.581
Well, sit down, Mr. Scamander.

00:06:53.959 --> 00:06:55.544
We're not gonna poison you.

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:57.171
(CREATURE SQUEAKS)

